From 953a962192aa82a4f72f03cf6f9a1a024e5502bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 05:25:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: correct POWERINFER_IOCP row - A/B was noise, direction
 UNRESOLVED

Self-correction. The previous row claimed "IOCP does not regress the read path"
off a +31% mean gap. That is an overclaim and the registry is the public
contract, so it gets fixed rather than left standing.

The arithmetic: between-arm mean gap is 1.35 t/s, but the within-arm spread of
the IOCP arm alone is 2.42->8.74 = 6.32 t/s. With one roll per cell, dropping
IOCP's best roll puts its mean at 4.63 and dropping its worst puts it at 6.74 -
straddling the sync mean of 4.31. A single data point moves the result across
the comparison, so there is no signal in either direction.

Verdict is now INDETERMINATE BOTH WAYS: neither a gain nor a regression is
established. This also retires the earlier "lean-suspicious" reading, which was
based on a flat-vs-plateau shape the A/B does not support.

Unchanged and still correct: correctness ON is proven (streaming engaged,
working set 4.77 GB vs an 11.4 GB model file, zero IOCP errors), and both the
ring-full and ERROR_IO_PENDING branches remain unexercised.

Ported-mechanism: n/a - measurement-record correction
Source-path: docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md
Evidence: research/local-inference/trial-evidence/110/run-journal.jsonl (verdict-correction-2)
Origin: ArifiLabs/iocp-async
---
 docs/OPTIONS-REGISTRY.md | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

